 temporary work tree, and initRepoCommit (951-971) runs git add --all, commit, and push, so the content becomes the initial commit of the new repository and is retrievable through the raw API. Forward-slash ../ input is neutralized by path.Clean, and the embed.FS fallback is protected by fs.ValidPath, so the reachable sink is the os.ReadFile(customPath) branch. On Linux and macOS, filepath.Join treats the backslash as a filename character, so this path is Windows-only. ## Impact On a Windows deployment, an authenticated user with repository-creation rights can read custom/conf/app.ini, disclosing SECRET_KEY and the database credentials, and can read any file that the Gogs process can read. SECRET_KEY is the source of the AES-GCM key used for two-factor secrets (MD5(SecretKey), see two_factor.go and two_factors.go), so its disclosure can enable decryption or forgery of those secrets when combined with other data. The read content is placed in the initial commit of the user's own repository and can be read back in full. ## Proof of Concept <details> <summary>Show the proof of concept</summary> Verified on commit dbbd717e923694c36f41b0360515b4374bbe6ee0. From a normal checkout of that commit, build and start the service: ```bash git checkout dbbd717e923694c36f41b0360515b4374bbe6ee0 CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build -tags prod -o gogs.exe ./cmd/gogs ./gogs.exe web ``` After registering the user and exchanging HTTP basic authentication for a personal access token, run reproduce.sh, whose source is inlined below: ```bash #!/usr/bin/env bash set -euo pipefail BASE=http://127.0.0.1:3000 AUTH='Authorization: token <sha>' echo 'Exploit-A' curl -sS -o /dev/null -w 'create=%{http_code}
